<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aryandes</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">6th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century-bce">6th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Aryandes was the Persian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/satrapy">satrap</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cambyses-ii">Cambyses II</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darius-i">Darius I</a> in the late 6th century BCE. At the request of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pheretime">Pheretime</a> of Cyrene he sent an army and fleet against Barca, which fell around 515 BCE after a long siege, and many of its people were deported to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bactria">Bactria</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herodotus">Herodotus</a> says Darius later had him executed for issuing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> coinage that rivalled the king's own.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/aryandes.jpg" alt="Aryandes" width="320" height="324" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mossmaps · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Western_part_of_the_Achaemenid_Empire.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
